# SymbiYosys job for eog_unpack (Verify role, task T1.unpack.fv). Properties: fv_eog_unpack.sv (P1-P5, B_*, covers).
#   bash scripts/formal.sh unpack          # all tasks, report in reports/formal_unpack.txt
#
# eog_unpack has no multiplier and no formal observation ports (conventions §7); see the harness header.
#
# prove : unbounded proof of every assertion with abc pdr (IC3), no environment constraints beyond the input
#         handshake. Why not k-induction: the DUT's beat position, partial record and REC_NO counter are invisible
#         at the ports until a record leaves, so with arbitrarily long idle stretches no induction depth closes
#         without internal invariants (tried: depth 30 still fails induction on P1_ghost / P4_last against a stub).
#         PDR learns the needed invariants itself. Against the verifier's throwaway stubs (never committed) on the
#         shared, loaded WSL machine: double-buffered stub PASS in 3-4.5 min, pass-through stub PASS in 36 s; seven
#         mutants FAIL in 2-3 s on the expected label (P2_recno, P3_byte, P4_fe x2, P4_last, B_rate, u_out.ax_hold).
# bmc   : smtbmc, every assertion from reset, depth 14 = reset + idle cycle + 12 beats (two full records) + output.
#         Quick counterexamples for the RTL author (80-90 s against the stubs); P3's data path makes each further
#         step about twice as slow, so the unbounded result comes from `prove`.
# cover : the spec's covers (two full records back to back; a framing error then a good record) + sanity covers.
#         Depth 24 (deepest goal, C1_b2b, is reached at step 13-14 against the stubs); ~1 s.

[tasks]
prove
bmc
cover

[options]
prove: mode prove
bmc:   mode bmc
bmc:   depth 14
cover: mode cover
cover: depth 24

[engines]
prove: abc pdr
bmc:   smtbmc boolector
cover: smtbmc yices

[script]
read_verilog -formal -sv eog_fv_props.sv
read_verilog -formal -sv -I . eog_unpack.sv
read_verilog -formal -sv -I . fv_eog_unpack.sv
prep -top fv_eog_unpack

[files]
../common/eog_fv_props.sv
../../rtl/eog_defs.svh
../../rtl/eog_unpack.sv
fv_eog_unpack.sv
